  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Tied through nine innings, they had the game in their hands in the tenth and still couldn't hold it.",
    "what_this_means": "A masterclass in what should have been. Carlos Rod\u00f3n carved through five innings without allowing a hit, striking out six, leaving the bullpen nothing but clean air. Paul Blackburn and David Bednar combined for four scoreless frames after that. Shutdown stuff when it mattered most. Amed Rosario broke a 2\u20132 tie in the tenth with a single, pushing New York ahead. Then Fernando Cruz walked onto the mound and immediately gave back three runs. That's the game. Dominant pitching, a moment of execution from Rosario, and then the bullpen forgot how to pitch when the margin was thinnest. They scored just three runs across ten innings. Enough to win if the back end held. It didn't. This team doesn't lose one-run games by accident. Every game in a division race that tight matters. They had this one. They wasted it.",
    "what_to_watch": "Detroit's Casey Mize comes in with a 2.95 ERA. That's exactly the kind of starter this lineup needs to prove something against tonight. Not a middling pitcher they can chase, but a true test of whether they can actually produce when it counts.",
